cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "longitudinal-health-foundation-model (LHFM)"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. LHFM is a research prototype: the public release is
  trained on synthetic data only and is not a medical device.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Olcan"
    given-names: "Ceyhun"
    # Replace with your ORCID once you have one, e.g.:
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ceyhunolcan/longitudinal-health-foundation-model"
abstract: >-
  Self-supervised multimodal foundation model over wearable, smartphone, and
  environmental signals for personalized behavioral-health risk prediction.
  Research prototype with a synthetic-data pipeline plus adapters for the
  GLOBEM (PhysioNet) and LifeSnaps (Zenodo/Kaggle) public cohorts. Includes
  integrated-gradients interpretability, participant-clustered bootstrap
  CIs, a subgroup-stratified fairness audit, and a climate-regime
  generalization eval. Not a medical device.
keywords:
  - foundation model
  - self-supervised learning
  - digital health
  - wearable sensors
  - passive sensing
  - climate health
  - computational psychiatry
  - fairness auditing
license: MIT
